1.. Presentation of the Fiscal Year 2026 Proposed Operating Budget (Acting Finance Director Bretthauer). 
(Estimated Time: 1 Hr.)
DISCUSS AND PROVIDE DIRECTION {\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fswiss\fprq2\fcharset0 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Acting Finance Director Libby Bretthauer provided background regarding the item, began the PowerPoint Presentation and responded to City Council questions.\line\line The following staff members provided the PowerPoint overview of their departmental budgets:\line\line\ul Information Technology\ulnone\line Information Technology Director Miguel Guardado presented.\line\line\pard City Manager Talyn Mirzakhanian, Senior Management Analyst Tatyana Roujenova-Peltekova, and Information Technology Director Guardado responded to City Council questions.\line\line\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\ul Community Development\ulnone\line Interim Community Development Director Michael Codron presented.\line\line Interim Community Development Director Codron, Planning Manager Adam Finestone and City Manager Mirzakhanian responded to City Council questions.\line\line Planning Manager Finestone announced a community meeting to discuss potential interim uses of the site, to be discussed at Project Pulse at the Manhattan Heights Park Community Center on May 21, 2025, at 6:00 PM.\line\line Communications and Civic Engagement Manager Alexandria Latragna, Interim Community Development Director Codron, City Manager Mirzakhanian, Acting Finance Director Bretthauer and Traffic Engineer Erik Zandvliet responded to City Council questions.\line\line\ul Police Department\ulnone\line On behalf of Police Chief Rachel Johnson, Police Captain Christian Eichenlaub presented.\line\line Acting Finance Director Bretthauer, Police Captain Eichenlaub and Police Chief Johnson responded to City Council questions.\line\line At 7:48 PM, the City Council recessed and reconvened at 8:01 PM with all City Councilmembers present.\line\line\cf1 Mayor Howorth opened the floor to public comments. The following individual(s) spoke:\line\line Stefan Kampe\line Paul Wafer\line Steven De Baets\line Jill Lamkin\line\line Seeing no further requests to speak, Mayor Howorth closed the floor to public comments.\cf0\line\line\ul Fire Department\ulnone\line Interim Fire Chief Mike Lang presented and responded to City Council questions.\line\line\ul Parks and Recreation\ulnone\line Parks and Recreation Director Mark Leyman presented.\line\line Parks and Recreation Director Leyman, Acting Finance Director Bretthauer, Public Works Director Erick Lee and Senior Recreation Manager Melissa McCollum responded to City Council questions.\line\line\ul Public Works\ulnone\line Public Works Director Lee presented.\line\line Public Works Director Lee, Acting Finance Director Bretthauer and Interim Community Development Director Codron responded to City Council questions.\line\line\ul Human Resources\ulnone\line Human Resources Director Lisa Jenkins presented.\line\line Human Resources Director Jenkins and Risk Manager Briza Morales responded to City Council questions.\line\line\ul Management Services\ulnone\line Communications and Civic Engagement Manager Latragna presented.\line\line City Manager Mirzakhanian continued the presentation.\line\line Communications and Civic Engagement Manager Latragna, City Manager Mirzakhanian and Human Resources Director Jenkins responded to City Council questions.\line\line\cf1 Mayor Howorth opened the floor to public comments. The following individual(s) spoke:\line\line Stefan Kampe\line Paul Wafer\line Steven De Baets\line Jill Lamkin\line\line Seeing no further requests to speak, Mayor Howorth closed the floor to public comments.\line\line Public Works Director Lee, Acting Finance Director Bretthauer, Human Resources Director Jenkins responded to City Council questions.\line\line\cf0\b The City Council received and filed the report.\b0\line\pard\line\cf1\i0\f1\par
